<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hendrik van Rheede</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1636–1691</span> · Also known as Hendrik Adriaan van Rheede tot Drakenstein</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hendrik van Rheede tot Drakenstein was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> official and naturalist who served as commander of Malabar from 1670 to 1677. He sponsored and directed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hortus-malabaricus">Hortus Malabaricus</a>, a twelve-volume study of the plants of the Malabar coast published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a> from 1678 to 1693, compiled with Indian physicians and scholars. He died at sea as the company's commissioner-general.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hendrik-van-rheede.jpg" alt="Hendrik van Rheede" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HenricusAdrianusVanRheede_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
